{"Docs":[{"DocType":1,"IsAmended":false,"IsUpdated":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocOrderId":127,"AmendedBy":[],"Notes":[],"Drafts":[],"ChunkGroupStartingNodeId":"OKMUCO2020_CH1GEPR","NodeDepth":2,"TitleHtml":"<div class=\"chunk-title\">§ 1-2. - Definitions and rules of construction.</div>","ShouldShowMiniToc":false,"Id":"OKMUCO2020_CH1GEPR_S1-2DERUCO","Title":"§ 1-2. - Definitions and rules of construction.","Content":"<div class=\"chunk-content\">\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               In the construction of this Code and of all ordinances, the following rules of construction\n               and definitions shall be observed, unless such construction or definition would be\n               inconsistent with the manifest intent of the Council, be repugnant to the context\n               of the provisions, or the context clearly requires otherwise:\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (1)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Charter</span> or <span class=\"ital\">City Charter.</span> When the term \"Charter\" or \"City Charter\" is used in this Code, such term shall be\n                  deemed to refer to the Charter of The City of Oklahoma City, as amended.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (2)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">City.</span> The words \"the City\" or \"this City\" shall be construed to mean The City of Oklahoma\n                  City, Oklahoma.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (3)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">City boundaries.</span> The term \"City boundaries\" or \"within the City\" shall include not only the corporate\n                  limits of the City, but also any property which it owns or which is under its jurisdiction.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (4)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Code.</span> The term \"Code\" or \"this Code\" shall be deemed to refer to the Oklahoma City Municipal\n                  Code, 2020, as established in <a href=\"\" data-chunk-id=\"OKMUCO2020_CH1GEPR_S1-1HOCODECI\" class=\"section-link\" data-product-id=\"17000\">Section 1-1</a> above.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (5)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Computation of time.</span> The time within which an act is to be done, when expressed in days, shall be computed\n                  by excluding the first day and excluding the last day if the last day be a Sunday\n                  or a legal holiday designated by the Council, and if the time is expressed in hours\n                  the whole of Sunday or of such legal holiday, from midnight to midnight, shall be\n                  excluded.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"refstatelaw0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>State Law reference— </b>\n                  Legal holidays, 25 O.S. § 82.1 et seq.\n                  </p>\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (6)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Council.</span> Whenever the words \"Council\" or \"City Council\" are used, they shall mean the Council\n                  of The City of Oklahoma City.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (7)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">County.</span> The word \"County\" shall mean Oklahoma County, Cleveland County, Canadian County,\n                  Logan County, Pottawatomie County or such other counties in which the City may be\n                  located, or any combination thereof, as appropriate.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (8)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Delegation of authority.</span> Whenever any authority, duty or other activity is charged to a City officer or employee,\n                  it may be done as well by such person's duly appointed agent, so long as not prohibited\n                  by ordinance, Charter or the laws or Constitution of the State, and so long as such\n                  officer or employee retains supervision over the discharge of the duly delegated authority,\n                  duty or activity.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (9)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Gender.</span> Every word importing the masculine gender shall extend to and be applied to the feminine\n                  gender and to the neuter gender unless the context clearly requires otherwise.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"refstatelaw0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>State Law reference— </b>\n                  Similar rule of statutory construction, 25 O.S. § 24.\n                  </p>\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (10)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Health Department.</span> The words \"Health Department\" shall mean the City-County Health Department created\n                  by agreement between the City and Oklahoma County pursuant to the provisions of 63\n                  O.S. § 1-214, as amended.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"refcross0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>Cross reference— </b>\n                  Health Department, <a href=\"\" data-chunk-id=\"OKMUCO2020_CH23HESA_ARTIIHEDE_S23-16CR\" class=\"section-link\" data-product-id=\"17000\">§ 23-16</a> et seq.\n                  </p>\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (11)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Joint authority.</span> Words giving a joint authority to three or more public officers or other persons\n                  shall be construed as giving such authority to a majority of them, unless clearly\n                  expressed otherwise.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"refstatelaw0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>State Law reference— </b>\n                  Similar rule of statutory construction, 25 O.S. § 31.\n                  </p>\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (12)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">May.</span> The word \"may\" is permissive.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (13)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Municipal Court.</span> The term \"Municipal Court\" shall have the meaning assigned to it in <a href=\"\" data-chunk-id=\"OKMUCO2020_CH33MUCO_ARTIINGE_S33-1CR\" class=\"section-link\" data-product-id=\"17000\">Section 33-1</a>.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (14)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Nontechnical and technical words.</span> Words and phrases shall be construed according to the common and approved usage of\n                  the language; but technical words and phrases and such others as may have acquired\n                  a peculiar and appropriate meaning in law shall be construed and understood according\n                  to such meaning.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (15)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Oath.</span> The word \"oath\" shall include an affirmation or declaration in all cases in which,\n                  by law, an affirmation may be substituted for an oath, and in those cases the words\n                  \"swear\" and \"sworn\" shall be the equivalent to the words \"affirm\" and \"affirmed.\"\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"refstatelaw0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>State Law reference— </b>\n                  Similar rule of statutory construction, 25 O.S. § 26.\n                  </p>\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (16)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Officers, departments, commissions, etc.</span> Whenever any officer, department or board or commission is referred to by title only,\n                  such reference shall be construed as if followed by the words \"of The City of Oklahoma\n                  City,\" unless the context clearly requires otherwise.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (17)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Oklahoma Statutes.</span> All references to the Oklahoma Statutes in this Code shall be deemed to refer to\n                  the latest edition of such statutes, as amended from time to time.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (18)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Or, and.</span> The word \"or\" may be read \"and.\" The word \"and\" may be read \"or\" if the sense requires\n                  it.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (19)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Ordinance.</span> The term \"ordinance\" shall mean an ordinance of The City of Oklahoma City, unless\n                  the context clearly requires otherwise.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (20)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Owner.</span> The word \"owner,\" applied to a building or land, shall include a person with any\n                  legal or beneficial interest in the property, including any part owner, joint owner,\n                  tenant in common, tenant in partnership, joint tenant or tenant by the entirety, of\n                  the whole or a part of the building or land.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (21)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Person.</span> The word \"person\" shall extend and be applied to firms, corporations and any other\n                  legal entity, voluntary associations, clubs, societies, trusts, or any other organization\n                  as well as to individuals, unless plainly inapplicable.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (22)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Preceding, following.</span> The words \"preceding\" and \"following\" shall mean next before and next after, respectively.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (23)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Property.</span> The word \"property\" shall include real and personal property.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"refstatelaw0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>State Law reference— </b>\n                  Similar rule of statutory construction, 25 O.S. § 26.\n                  </p>\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (24)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Shall.</span> The word \"shall\" is mandatory.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (25)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Sidewalk.</span> The word \"sidewalk\" shall mean that portion of a street between the curbline and\n                  the adjacent property intended for the use of pedestrians.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (26)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Singular and plural.</span> Words in the plural include the singular, and vice versa.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"refstatelaw0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>State Law reference— </b>\n                  Similar rule of statutory construction, 25 O.S. § 25.\n                  </p>\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (27)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">State.</span> The words \"the State\" or \"this State\" shall be construed to mean the State of Oklahoma.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (28)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Street.</span> The word \"street\" shall include any public ways, roads, highways, avenues, alleys\n                  and lanes within the City.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (29)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Supervisor of Licenses.</span> The term \"Supervisor of Licenses\" shall refer to that City officer or employee whose\n                  function it is to issue licenses for the City.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (30)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Tenant, occupant.</span> The words \"tenant\" and \"occupant,\" when applied to a building or land, shall include\n                  any person who occupies or is in possession of the whole or part of such building\n                  or land, whether alone or with others.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (31)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Week.</span> The word \"week\" shall be construed to mean seven days. Publication in a newspaper\n                  of any notice or other matter indicated to be for a stated number of weeks shall be\n                  construed to mean one insertion each week, unless specifically stated to be for each\n                  day of the week or for more than one day in each week; all publications heretofore\n                  made in accordance with the terms of this sentence are hereby validated.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (32)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Writing.</span> The word \"writing\" shall include any representation of words, letters or figures,\n                  whether by printing or otherwise.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"refstatelaw0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>State Law reference— </b>\n                  Similar rule of statutory construction, 25 O.S. § 28.\n                  </p>\n               \n               <p class=\"incr1\">\n                  (33)\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"content2\">\n                  <span class=\"ital\">Year.</span> The word \"year\" shall mean a calendar year.\n                  </p>\n               \t\t\n               <p class=\"refstatelaw0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>State Law reference— </b>\n                  Similar rule of statutory construction, 25 O.S. § 23.\n                  </p>\n               \n            <p class=\"historynote0\">\n               (Code 1970, §§ 1-2, 1-4; Code 1980, § 1-2; Ord. No. 18621, § 1, 11-4-86; Ord. No.\n               22540, § 1, 9-14-04)\n               </p></div>","SortDate":null,"Footnotes":null}],"NewOrds":[],"PdfUrl":null,"LastOrd":null,"PrevNode":{"Id":"OKMUCO2020_CH1GEPR_S1-1HOCODECI","Heading":"§ 1-1. - How Code designated and cited.","NodeDepth":2,"HasChildren":false,"ParentId":"OKMUCO2020_CH1GEPR","DocOrderId":126,"Children":[],"Data":{"NodeKey":null,"IsUpdated":false,"IsAmended":false,"HasAmendedDescendant":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocType":1,"DepthOverride":null,"ChunkGroupStartingId":null}},"NextNode":{"Id":"OKMUCO2020_CH1GEPR_S1-3RECOCO","Heading":"§ 1-3. - References to Code; conflicts.","NodeDepth":2,"HasChildren":false,"ParentId":"OKMUCO2020_CH1GEPR","DocOrderId":128,"Children":[],"Data":{"NodeKey":null,"IsUpdated":false,"IsAmended":false,"HasAmendedDescendant":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocType":1,"DepthOverride":null,"ChunkGroupStartingId":null}},"ShowToc":false}